<title>FRANCE: France near 1996/97 wheat export goal - ONIC.</title>
<headline>France near 1996/97 wheat export goal - ONIC.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>France is close to meeting its target to export 6.4 million tonnes of soft wheat to countries outside the European Union in 1996/97, the head of national grain office ONIC said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Including wheat sales to Iraq, French soft wheat export commitments currently stand at 6.3 million tonnes, director general Alain Moulinier told a news conference.</p>
<p>&quot;There are still 100,000 tonnes left, provided there are no delays on Iraq (sales),&quot; he said.</p>
<p>The United Nations has already cleared the export of 325,000 tonnes of French soft wheat to Iraq out of total sales of over 600,000 tonnes under the oil-for-food pact.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
